**Root cause:** In `Fraction.greatestCommonDivisor(int u, int v)`, the initial short-circuit check `Math.abs(u) <= 1 || Math.abs(v) <= 1` mishandled `Integer.MIN_VALUE`: `Math.abs(Integer.MIN_VALUE)` overflows back to `Integer.MIN_VALUE` (still negative), which is `<= 1`, so the method incorrectly returned a GCD of 1 whenever one of the operands was `Integer.MIN_VALUE`. This caused `getReducedFraction(Integer.MIN_VALUE, 2)` and `Fraction(Integer.MIN_VALUE, 2).reduce()` to skip reduction entirely, leaving the numerator as `Integer.MIN_VALUE` instead of the correctly reduced `Integer.MIN_VALUE / 2`.

**Fix:** Changed the guard in `src/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/math/Fraction.java` to compare the values directly against `1` and `-1` instead of using `Math.abs`, avoiding the overflow:

```java
if (u == 1 || u == -1 || v == 1 || v == -1) {
    return 1;
}
```
